 ## Change Log
 
 ### 2026-05-03
+- `mm_sport_v1` / MM 2.0 discovery pressure control: changed discovery to full snapshot on startup, scheduled full refresh every 6 hours, 2-page delta refresh every 1 hour, capped reward detail fan-out, hardened sticky WS caps, and starts fresh-BUY cooldown when WS reports an expired quote as terminal canceled (`src/mm/mod.rs`, `src/main.rs`, `src/polymarket_ws.rs`, `.env.example`, `.env.full.example`, `docs/mm_sport_v1.md`).
+  - Applies to Sport, Non-S, and Dual routes. Discovery cache can stay broader than the active quote cap, but CLOB detail work and WS scope are bounded so stale reward rows do not inflate CPU/socket load.
 - `mm_sport_v1` / MM 2.0 route baseline feasibility: fixed the paired quote feasibility guard so Multiple markets use the active Sport/Non-S route multiplier, while Depth Ratio markets keep the configured baseline multiplier (`src/main.rs`).
   - Affects Sport, Non-S, and Dual route fresh BUY entry only; exits, cancels, FIFO, and inventory cleanup are unchanged.
 - `mm_sport_v1` / MM 2.0 active-market and churn controls: added route-aware fresh-entry caps, independent FIFO depth ratio, randomized fresh-BUY cooldown after FIFO cancel or natural quote expiry, and hard reconcile for uncertain pending orders (`src/mm/mod.rs`, `src/main.rs`, `.env.example`, `.env.full.example`, `docs/mm_sport_v1.md`).
